cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the OIP specification or its reference code, please cite this repository and the commit you used."
title: "OIP: Oracle Interoperability Protocol specification and reference implementation"
abstract: >-
  OIP, the Oracle Interoperability Protocol, defines message semantics,
  state transitions, routing, validation, errors and conformance rules for
  state-machine implementations that change state across chains and
  off-chain systems. Version 0.6.0 specifies a signed protobuf message (wire
  version 6), the checks a receiver applies before any effect, and the
  recorded outcome of each of its 31 operations. The repository includes a
  Rust reference implementation and a Go message layer, both generated from
  one schema and tested against shared vectors.
type: software
